 which you can and should checkout. *","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-14-2022, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T10:09:20-08:00","id":1497185,"title":"","content":"Can\u2019t wait to see them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T12:33:41-08:00","id":1497202,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Nimbus Spinners</b></span><br /> A legacy of Nimbus Artists<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames</b>: The Crowned, Coronals, Spinners, Pollyannas (Derogatory)<br /> <b>Organization</b>: The Spinners are often social, and many maintain regular contact with other Spinners, to discuss techniques, new Nimbus related phenomena or to give and receive criticism. Small groups sometimes form, but many prefer to do their actual work by themselves. A dedicated cabal is unheard of, many instead attach themselves to other cabals.<br /> <br /> Many Spinners are involved in the trade of Magic Services, adding decorations only visible to Mage Sight to Sanctums and examining and advising others on shaping the Nimbus. some even act as detectives, deducing how and why a mysterious Nimbus appears the way it does.<br /> <b>Theory</b>: The Nimbus is the most Sublime Medium<br /> <b>Background</b>: The legacy is thought to quite old, but little remains of the original Artworks. The Legacy's modern origins are traced to a Nimbus weaved Banner, containing the combined Nimbuses of a Cabal. Many Members of the Legacy are eccentric, due to the requirements of methods of shaping their own Nimbus. Anyone can join the legacy, as the Initiation is well know to the boarder Awakened community.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Obrimos; Free Council, Silver Ladder<br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Prime<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Thematic Nimbus Imprints (+1), Mundane Artist Tools(+1), Imago Modifies or examines the Nimbus (+1), success on an Expression roll relating to the spell (+2)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Detailed Planning of New Art, Examining a New Nimbus, Giving Heartfelt Artistic Criticism<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Taste (Nimbus Art), Expression 2, Occult Specialty (Nimbus)<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Creating your first Nimbus Art, and Scrutinizing it<br /> <br /> <i>Artist\u2019s Eye</i><br /> (Prime \u25cf) <u>Initiation</u><br /> Working deeply with Nimbuses gives an Spinner insight into what gives the Nimbus it's form.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><i> Nimbus Tuning</i></u><br /> Potency = Prime<br /> Duration = N/A (1)<br /> Scale = All extra factors to Scale<br /> Range = Touch<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> COMMENTARY: The artist should know their paints<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Space \u25cf)<br /> One Learns quickly that the canvas is almost as Important to Artwork as the Artwork itself<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10p